I'm not dusting the blonde.

255
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,400
I'm just putting her on hold till next week, all right?

256
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,760
Hey, Eddie, here, tell me what it sounds like, okay?

257
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:59,900
Hi. Call me crazy, but this just can't wait.

258
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:03,640
You know, I think that we've got something really special here between us.

259
00:14:03,740 --> 00:14:06,820
And I don't want to share that with a bunch of high school kids in dance.

260
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:09,980
So, how do you say you and me go on instead next week?

261
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:11,060
Just the two of us.

262
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:25,200
Hi. Hi. Look, uh, call me crazy, but this just couldn't wait.

263
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:27,320
You know, I think we've got something real...

264
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:30,240
Hi, Elaine. Something really special.

265
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:33,940
It could wait after all.

266
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:44,980
I'm sorry. You can talk to him in here till recess, Ed.

267
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:49,620
Thanks. Boy, when you're small, people don't even ask you if you want your parents

268
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:52,960
called. So I understand you want to be transferred to another school.

269
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:55,960
Yeah, well, this place is getting kind of old.

270
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,960
Well, that would be difficult.

271
00:14:58,060 --> 00:15:00,820
You see, for you to go to another school, we've got to move to another district.

272
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:02,160
Is that a problem?

273
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:05,580
Yes. I got it.

274
00:15:05,660 --> 00:15:06,840
How about Hebrew school?

275
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:11,240
How about you telling me why some kid wants to fight with you?

276
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,480
You heard? Mm -hmm.

277
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:18,500
See, there's this big mean kid, Louis Vasco, and last year I wouldn't let him cheat

278
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:20,240
off me. Well, good for you.

279
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:21,720
He sent a message.

280
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:23,520
Three o 'clock for his bathroom.

281
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:27,980
Ben, this is so strange.

282
00:15:29,860 --> 00:15:31,940
Well, it wouldn't meet me in the girls' bathroom.

283
00:15:31,940 --> 00:15:34,260
No, I mean this whole situation.

284
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:36,920
Would you believe the same thing happened to me?

285
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:38,460
Come on, Dad.

286
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:39,960
You don't believe me?

287
00:15:40,060 --> 00:15:44,900
You're going to do like you always do and tell me some story of how you didn't run

288
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:46,620
and you ended up being friends.

289
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:48,900
No, I ran.

290
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:53,420
What? I was 11 years old and I was trying out for this baseball team, the Oilers.

291
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:57,480
Well, it came right down to me or this other boy for the third base position, see?

292
00:15:58,140 --> 00:15:59,580
Well, boy wasn't really right.

293
00:15:59,580 --> 00:16:00,800
This kid was a gorilla.

294
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:02,600
They call him Killer.

295
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,440
What'd you do?

296
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:08,640
I quit. I didn't play baseball that whole year.

297
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:14,680
Anyway, I didn't see Killer again for, well, 15 years.

298
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:16,380
And I saw him at a reunion.

299
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:18,240
He had a big beer belly.

300
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:21,220
All athletes end up with beer bellies.

301
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:27,340
And I was there with your mom, and Killer, whose real name was Ralph, he was, uh...

302
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:28,580
Dad, what's your point?

303
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:32,920
Well, the point is, he told me he was glad that I didn't fight him that day.

304
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:36,840
Why? Because he was just as afraid of me as I was of him.

305
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,800
Big guys are afraid, too?

306
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:44,520
Yes. So you're saying I should face this guy like a man?

307
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:49,580
That's right. Then if that doesn't work and he starts to hit you, then you run like

308
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:54,400
the wind. Excuse me, do my chas have a date for tonight's dance?

309
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:57,160
Pardon me, but I, uh...

310
00:16:57,160 --> 00:17:00,940
Hi. Why won't anyone go to the dance?

311
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:03,040
Oh, sorry, Carol.

312
00:17:03,180 --> 00:17:04,660
I thought you was just a regular girl.

313
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:05,800
2 p.m.

314
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:07,340
and things are not getting better.

315
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:09,760
I give up.

316
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:12,300
I'm sorry. I thought I'd try something new, but it didn't work.

317
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:14,040
Tell me about it.

318
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:15,880
Nothing ever changes for me.

319
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:21,080
Mona? I know exactly how you feel.

320
00:17:21,500 --> 00:17:22,520
I'm like dog drool.

321
00:17:26,080 --> 00:17:28,960
I was expecting today to be different too.

322
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:31,460
I was stupid enough to even think I could get a date.

323
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:35,960
All I wanted was something new, something different,

324
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:38,000
something unusual.

325
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,560
If I am...

326
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:47,100
Did agree to go on this dance with you, which I haven't.

327
00:17:47,140 --> 00:17:48,860
Right, right, right.

328
00:17:50,140 --> 00:17:51,780
You'd have to agree to certain conditions.

329
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:54,280
Anything. No hand holding.

330
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:56,480
No slow dancing.

331
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:57,960
No fast dancing.

332
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:01,560
And if you agree to go with me, I don't even have to show up.

333
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:03,280
Do I? No.

334
00:18:04,540 --> 00:18:06,340
Okay, you've got your date.

335
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:09,660
And you got something unusual.

336
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:54,640
I'm sorry. I hear you've been looking for me.

337
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:57,480
Yeah? So I'm here.

338
00:18:58,060 --> 00:18:58,720
What's the matter?

339
00:18:59,020 --> 00:18:59,840
Afraid to come in?

340
00:19:00,140 --> 00:19:01,920
You're afraid to come out!

341
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:08,340
Louis? Hey, Dad was right.

342
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:10,680
Alright, you little...

343
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:13,060
You... you grew.

344
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:16,560
You didn't. I think that's my bus.

345
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:22,260
I'm sorry. Oh, Ben, he was actually afraid of you.

346
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:26,300
Yeah, well, Mark, everybody's a little bit afraid.

347
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:28,060
Even big guys like me.

348
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:32,340
Now, I don't want to break Elaine's heart, and I sure don't want to upset the

349
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:34,700
blonde. So, uh, it's out of my hands.

350
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:37,060
Now, the next girl that walks around the corner is history.

351
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:40,160
Whistle. Whistle. Ha -ha.

352
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:41,240
Boner. Boner. I know.

353
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:45,300
Get lost. What?

354
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,840
What happened? Uh, gym class.

355
00:19:47,980 --> 00:19:49,680
I, uh, I misfired on a power squat.

356
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:54,940
Yeah, um, look, I have to see a doctor, uh, tonight.

357
00:19:55,460 --> 00:19:56,620
So the dance is out?

358
00:19:56,720 --> 00:20:00,700
Yeah. I -I am really sorry, Lane, but I promise we will go out just as soon as I'm

359
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:03,380
whole. I hope you understand.

360
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:04,860
Of course I do.

361
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:06,640
Is there anything I can do to help?

362
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:09,760
No. No, I'd rather not have you see me like this, okay?

363
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:11,780
Okay. Um, take care.

364
00:20:11,780 --> 00:20:13,600
You too. Bye -bye.

365
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:20,580
Hi. You! Me.

366
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:28,700
Look, I'm a class dude, and I don't want to meet my date at the dance, so what do

367
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:29,680
you say I pick you up?

368
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:32,180
Date? We don't have a date.

369
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,420
Yes, we do for the dance tonight.

370
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:36,820
No, I just said I'd see you there.

371
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,120
Oh, wait a minute.

372
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,000
I get it.

373
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,360
You found someone you like better and you dumped me, huh?

374
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:45,540
Oh, no, I could never do something like that, could you?

375
00:20:47,340 --> 00:20:50,040
Ah, you changed the subject here.

376
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:51,720
Mike, you misunderstood.

377
00:20:52,040 --> 00:20:53,280
Misunderstood? Are you...

378
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:55,160
Do you have any idea what I gave up for you?

379
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:56,740
I didn't ask you to give anything up.

380
00:20:56,740 --> 00:20:57,600
I'll tell you what.

381
00:20:57,600 --> 00:21:00,040
I gave up Elaine Dooley for a date with you.

382
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:07,120
Mike, I couldn't date you.

383
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:08,880
I don't even trust you.

384
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:13,300
Look, before you mistrust me, I suggest you get to know me.

385
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:16,520
I do know you, Mike.

386
00:21:16,660 --> 00:21:19,500
From where? Do you remember the class picnic last year?

387
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:21,040
No, no, no, you weren't there.

388
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:22,100
I would have remembered you.

389
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:23,500
I can prove I was there.

390
00:21:23,820 --> 00:21:28,240
You did that really funny impression of Bucktooth Becky's work, and remember?

391
00:21:29,060 --> 00:21:31,220
Ha. Pass the corn, please.

392
00:21:32,140 --> 00:21:33,540
Very funny. Ha -ha.

393
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:40,560
Becky? Oh, you have had quite a summer.

394
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:43,600
And you have had quite a fall.

395
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:52,020
Hi, guys. Hi.

396
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:55,780
Hi. So, Jason, were you lonely today?

397
00:21:56,900 --> 00:22:03,300
Uh -huh. And, Ben, what did you learn your first day back?

398
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:06,400
I learned that Hebrew school is not the answer.

399
00:22:06,820 --> 00:22:09,280
That's true. I'll explain later.

400
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:17,320
So, Carol, was today everything you hoped it would be?

401
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:20,640
Well, it started out a little shaky, but it ended up okay.

402
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:23,540
Ah, good. I even have a date for dance.

403
00:22:24,400 --> 00:22:28,880
Great! And the best part is, I don't even have to go.

404
00:22:33,700 --> 00:22:37,120
Oh. Mike, you're late.

405
00:22:37,180 --> 00:22:37,840
Where have you been?

406
00:22:38,140 --> 00:22:39,560
Mom, I've been doing some thinking.

407
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:42,460
Girls have feelings just like regular people.

408
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:48,100
Uh -huh. You know, Mom, I think I have learned more today than I have in my entire

409
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:51,320
educational career. Well, that's great, Mike.

410
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:52,600
So you have good teachers?

411
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:55,480
Uh, maybe. I'll find out tomorrow when I go to class.

412
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:04,900
Jason? Ben? Mike, seven o 'clock comes early.

413
00:23:04,940 --> 00:23:05,760
Let's go, pal.

414
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:11,240
All right. Carol, honey, school in the morning.

415
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:15,160
All right. Ben, you're long overdue.

416
00:23:15,260 --> 00:23:16,460
Lights out now.

417
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:19,000
No way. I'm afraid of the dark.

418
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:21,060
You know, Ben, this is interesting.

419
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:24,480
When I was your age, I too was...

420
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:26,400
Ben? Forget it, Dad.

421
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:27,560
I love the dark.

422
00:23:52,920 --> 00:23:53,660
I'm gonna be a good boy.

423
00:23:58,780 --> 00:23:59,440
I'm gonna be a good boy.
